JavaGames

This is a collection of simple games written in Java programming language. The
games are compiled into Java applets and are meant to be player on-line in web
browser. Games are free and released under GPL license - see file COPYING for
details.

Currently the collection contains four games:

1. XO World

Game similar to tic-tac-toe. You play against computer on 10x10 board. Both you
and opponent place signs (yours is X, and computer's is O) on the board - one
at a time. The goal is to make a line of 5 signs before your opponent. Lines
can be horizontal, vertical or diagonal.


2. 100 Mack

Computer makes random combination of 4 images out of set of six and you need to
guess that combination. Set the desired combination and computer will compare
it with combination that you need to guess and show you two types of marks:
either a hit, or correct image, but at wrong position.


3. Memory

In this simple memory game, there are 36 plates with 18 diferrent pictures on
them. You can flip 2 plates at a time, and need to find two that match. When
you match the plates, they vanish from the screen. The goal of the game is to
clear all fields, making the least possible number of flips. There is also a
two-player mode, where you need to match more pairs than your opponent.


4. Tetris

This is plain old tetris game. Various shapes fall from the top and you need to
move and rotate them to fit them at the bottom as best as you can. When you
fill up a horizontal line, it gets removed from the heap. The game advances to
next level when you remove enough lines.

